  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 1243 AM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nTemperatures drop significantly with the loss of daytime heating on \nWednesday night through Thursday morning. A good setup is in store \nfor radiational cooling with light winds and clear skies for another \nfreezing night across portions of the southern Edwards Plateau, Hill \nCountry, I-35 corridor, and the Coastal Plains. Latest MOS guidance \nruns bring colder temperatures than the NBM for these locations. \nTherefore, this forecast shows data from the CONSMOS solution and \nsome local adjustments. Another Freeze Warning is likely issued \nsometime Wednesday if this trend continues.\n\nThanksgiving Day will be cool with highs in the 50s and 60s under \npartly cloudy skies. Another cool night awaits for the Hill Country \nwith lows in the low 30s and mid to upper 30s elsewhere. By Friday, \nsurface southerly flow is in place to warm temperatures into the 60s \nalmost everywhere with the exception of higher elevations. The \nwarming trend continues into the weekend with dry conditions and \nhighs in the mid to upper 60s and low 70s.",
